#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163004} :activity/id #uuid "c9745592-4ec7-557a-9119-d1dcdcf23d32" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049149 :topic/id #uuid "de945224-de03-5292-84ca-39d9ddf3f7e4" :topic/math-academy-id 3003} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163004 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163288 :tutorial/content "Let's recall the multiplication law for conditional probability for two events ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](images/5d/5d8b650b90c85fbc0db5e4b6fae61767e293a843d18a2526f3ee4157733e1f4b.svg) ![](images/44/44229a2a35108e36c1348009a552be50e798af9b2807f49c4e4ef8515ed7eefe.svg)\n\nNow suppose that ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) are discrete random variables. The conditional probability that ![](images/2c/2cc57b1c8b00862c078193ea1774f4012e1513ab1a26a6d5bb806e046220a812.svg) *given that* ![](images/46/46851627a248368806191a89ed2bb59d72b83b2e352f768da26f41305e156052.svg) follows immediately from the multiplication law and is given by\n\n![](images/2b/2b705d0acedbb080625148287647d075dce75f40531615a52352a848a85892fe.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/a2/a2dcac06a4cf671df0fa43cef1727449fb2ebc57fb824d19cc07da5e75d12176.svg) is the joint PMF of ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/07/07fd689b67975f50da1b6b025460996fc87f21f758f5e98d34eb84c9b0e50fcd.svg) and ![](images/3a/3aa9c47fc054317f2163393853c05d71714e0c9f0424297f51b46b107e222229.svg) is the marginal mass function of ![](images/02/029615e92d8b6d5c444a4daf74a9a8d63048e8d4be5f97c8207fe7af2e189e18.svg)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- To avoid getting a zero in the denominator, this formula assumes that ![](images/f4/f40e8e149f4e148b5042516dae366a5d17bdc00e1d6e39e27ddf30ece6801d6f.svg)\n- If ![](images/0f/0fa3deb4b6345d48bdeeb06c02ecd3d9bcf6a68cf517412b251a2bcf1e67d07f.svg) then ![](images/ad/ad17cd2272c82a9380977e2ef9ff99fb613681da7df20c06949db320c701bc4c.svg) is not defined by the usual conditional probability formula, since the denominator is zero. In this discrete setting, we therefore restrict the formula to values of ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) for which ![](images/1e/1ebc42b48118a4c62d7203d91e76ecc1a865f8d536cf145c82499ac8fd531cc7.svg)\n\nIn a similar manner, the conditional probability that ![](images/46/46851627a248368806191a89ed2bb59d72b83b2e352f768da26f41305e156052.svg) given that ![](images/2c/2cc57b1c8b00862c078193ea1774f4012e1513ab1a26a6d5bb806e046220a812.svg) can be calculated as ![](images/8c/8c8bdddcd02a672d59ded44b5281cf2f24236f88b2f494730bac998a760e9b0a.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/fd/fdb49440ceb7e11cd9ba0b0869a1e6d3565549969180830d1796db7dd00a2b96.svg) is the marginal mass function of ![](images/ed/ed6dc1fd057e3dd2207c735a562bf4db22b72d1a9380651607439f00c0440725.svg) This formula assumes that ![](images/f8/f8020df80e303daf760cd9bf4d8437cc08bc4b95b0ccf64bc7a43ccddc650f5f.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "e69256ce-d99e-579e-a7f6-fbd459a410eb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5616 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "7df83356-4053-5631-85dc-83521ae0811d" :step/math-academy-id 34578 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163011}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163011 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162076 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161876 :question/id #uuid "ddfe8dda-9ab2-5b11-af30-159a7bd32d64" :question/math-academy-id "e-9256"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87675618-337f-5af2-8ad7-9132c080785a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048325} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050108}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162315} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162372} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363245} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363259} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363266} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363273}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"} :step/id #uuid "b56cb5f1-be37-5c19-a08d-76523e8ff1db" :step/math-academy-id 34630 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163012}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163012 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162077 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161877 :question/id #uuid "531b9a19-e424-59e5-8c02-7bca4f67e110" :question/math-academy-id "e-9258"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "348dfcb8-2325-5929-b622-5423b7e37a53" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162318} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162377} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362880} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363308} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363328}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Over an Interval"} :step/id #uuid "56d2a08f-a2e0-5602-b510-59f2481df9af" :step/math-academy-id 34637 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163067}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163065 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162104 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161670 :question/id #uuid "2afabb9d-bd38-50f1-9afd-710ab839163c" :question/math-academy-id "e-10049"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebabf742-2b8d-5392-a077-f34e8f4bd034" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162317} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162374} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363335} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363342} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363349} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400965} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400972}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Mass Function"} :step/id #uuid "000582c8-50ec-5bfc-b34a-c1cec0a03e2c" :step/math-academy-id 37921} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163066 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161671 :question/id #uuid "0e42cf0f-f1bd-5762-a4fc-3cedec697c14" :question/math-academy-id "e-10050"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162316} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162373} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363280} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363287} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363294} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363315}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"} :step/id #uuid "f16763f3-a2e5-5d38-9f53-ce65ea110dc5" :step/math-academy-id 37922 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163067 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163325 :tutorial/content "We can now define two more probability mass functions as follows:\n\n- The **conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$,** denoted $f_{X|Y}(x|y),$ is defined as $$f_{X|Y}(x|y) = P(X = x \\,|\\, Y = y) = \\dfrac{P(X = x, \\, Y = y)}{P(Y=y)} = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)},$$ where $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_Y(y)$ is the marginal mass function of $Y.$\n\n- The **conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x,$** denoted $f_{Y|X}(y|x),$ is defined as $$f_{Y|X}(y|x) = P(Y = y \\,|\\, X = x) = \\dfrac{P(X = x,\\, Y = y)}{P(X=x)} = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)},$$ where $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_X(x)$ is the marginal mass function of $X.$\n\n**Watch out!** The conditional distribution of $X$ given $Y$ does *not* equal the conditional distribution of $Y$ given $X$. That is, in general,\n\n$$f_{X|Y}(x|y) \\ne f_{Y|X}(y|x).$$\n\nFinally, if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then\n\n$$f_{X|Y}(x|y)=f_X(x),\\qquad f_{Y|X}(y|x)=f_Y(y).$$\n\nIn other words, if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then knowing the value of one random variable does not affect the probability distribution of the other." :tutorial/id #uuid "1cbdc2c5-105c-5f9a-b4f4-7e4651bdc789" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6273 :tutorial/title "Conditional Probability Mass Functions"} :step/id #uuid "acc71c94-7794-57f0-bfff-16c3d8ed9e31" :step/math-academy-id 38019 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163066}}] :activity/title "Conditional Distributions for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186162164}]}
